# 5. Login rate limiting: brute-force protection, 5 login attempts per minute per IP, then 429.
#
# VS Code "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" above each request.
# Logins from the other files in the last minute count too, so the 429 may come early.
# After this file, wait 1 minute before logging in again.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@api = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1
@adminEmail = {{$dotenv ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@adminPassword = {{$dotenv ADMIN_PASSWORD}}


### Brute force: send this several times → 401, 401, ... then 429 with a Retry-After header
# The 401 says "Invalid email or password." whether the email exists or not.
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Correct password while blocked → still 429 (the limit counts attempts, not failures)
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}
